Mod Roles

Purpose

Each major technology mod has a defined role within the progression of the pack.

The purpose of this system is to prevent mods from competing for the same progression space, while allowing them to complement each other through materials, machines, automation, logistics, power systems, exploration, and advanced production.

No mod should independently invalidate the main progression.

GregTech

GregTech is the primary technology progression system of the pack.

Its progression defines the main industrial path from the early electrical tiers through the highest conventional technology tiers.

GregTech is responsible for:

Material progression

Machine progression

Electrical tier progression

Advanced chemical processing

Complex industrial chains

High-tier components

Large-scale industrial infrastructure

Extreme endgame production

GregTech should provide the main progression gates for LV, MV, HV, EV, IV, LuV, ZPM, UV, and UHV.

Higher-tier GregTech machines and materials should require infrastructure from previous stages of the progression.

GregTech should remain the backbone of the industrial progression without becoming the only useful technology mod.

Modern Industrialization

Modern Industrialization is a complementary industrial technology system.

It provides additional machines, processing chains, automation systems, and industrial infrastructure that integrate with the main GregTech progression.

Modern Industrialization should:

Provide alternative or complementary processing systems

Expand industrial automation

Provide additional machines for specific production chains

Create cross-mod processing chains

Provide additional industrial infrastructure

Support large-scale production

Modern Industrialization must follow the same material and technology progression as the main pack.

It must not provide an easier route around major GregTech progression gates.

Its machines and materials should be integrated into the appropriate progression tiers.

Create

Create is the primary mechanical engineering and logistics system.

Create represents mechanical automation, transportation, physical infrastructure, and early industrial engineering.

Create should be especially important during the Primitive and Steam Ages, while remaining useful throughout the entire progression.

Create is responsible for:

Mechanical power

Mechanical automation

Item transportation

Material transportation

Physical logistics

Factory infrastructure

Mechanical processing

Large-scale material handling

Create should provide solutions to logistical and mechanical problems rather than replace electrical technology progression.

Create systems may interact with GregTech, Modern Industrialization, Mekanism, and other technologies through custom recipes and integrated production chains.

Create should remain useful even after electrical technology becomes dominant.

Mekanism

Mekanism is a supporting industrial technology system.

It provides advanced processing, chemical systems, utilities, energy infrastructure, and specialized industrial machinery.

Mekanism should complement rather than replace GregTech and Modern Industrialization.

Mekanism is responsible for:

Advanced material processing

Chemical processing

Specialized industrial machinery

Energy systems

Utility infrastructure

High-throughput processing

Advanced automation support

Mekanism processing chains may be integrated into higher-tier production requirements.

Mekanism must not provide an unrestricted shortcut to materials that are intended to require progression through GregTech or Modern Industrialization.

Applied Energistics 2

Applied Energistics 2 is the primary advanced logistics and storage system.

AE2 should represent the transition from physical logistics to highly advanced digital logistics.

AE2 is responsible for:

Digital storage

Automated item transportation

Automated crafting

Factory logistics

Large-scale resource management

Production monitoring

Complex automation networks

AE2 should become increasingly important as industrial complexity increases.

Its progression should be gated so that advanced storage, automation, and crafting systems require appropriate technological infrastructure.

AE2 should not eliminate the need for physical production infrastructure.

Factories must still require machines, power, resources, processing chains, and production capacity.

Create Aeronautics

Create Aeronautics is the primary advanced mechanical aviation and aerial engineering system.

It should expand the progression beyond conventional ground-based industrial infrastructure.

Create Aeronautics is responsible for:

Advanced aerial engineering

Mechanical aircraft systems

Aerial transportation

Large-scale mobile infrastructure

Advanced mechanical construction

Exploration through technological aviation

Create Aeronautics should become more relevant as the technological progression advances.

Its advanced systems should require materials and components from appropriate industrial tiers.

Aerial technology should expand exploration and transportation without bypassing the main technological progression.

Create Big Cannons

Create Big Cannons is the primary advanced artillery and heavy mechanical weapon engineering system.

It represents the development of large-scale industrial weaponry and military engineering.

Create Big Cannons is responsible for:

Heavy artillery

Large-scale mechanical weaponry

Advanced ammunition production

Industrial weapon manufacturing

Large-scale defensive infrastructure

Its progression should depend on industrial materials, mechanical infrastructure, and advanced manufacturing.

Create Big Cannons should not become an independent shortcut through the technological progression.

Advanced artillery and ammunition should require increasingly advanced industrial infrastructure.

Cross-Mod Role

The major technology mods are designed to complement each other.

GregTech defines the main technological progression.

Modern Industrialization expands industrial processing and automation.

Create provides mechanical engineering and physical logistics.

Mekanism provides specialized processing, chemistry, energy systems, and industrial utilities.

Applied Energistics 2 provides advanced digital logistics and automation.

Create Aeronautics provides advanced aerial engineering and transportation.

Create Big Cannons provides heavy mechanical engineering and industrial artillery.

Each system should solve different problems while sharing materials, infrastructure, resources, and progression requirements.

Cross-Mod Integration

Major progression components should frequently require systems from multiple mods.

Advanced GregTech components may require materials processed through Modern Industrialization or Mekanism.

Large factories may require Create logistics.

Late-game automation may require Applied Energistics 2.

Advanced aerial systems may require GregTech and Create infrastructure.

Advanced artillery may require Create, GregTech, and industrial manufacturing systems.

The exact dependencies will be defined during the Integration and Recipe Changes stages.

Progression Rule

No major mod should provide a complete alternative progression path to the endgame.

Mods may provide alternative methods of processing, automation, transportation, or infrastructure.

However, the overall progression must remain interconnected.

Advancing through the pack should require the player to understand and combine multiple technological systems rather than selecting one mod and ignoring the rest.

Final Goal

The technology system should feel like one interconnected industrial civilization rather than several independent mods placed together.

Every major mod should have a clear purpose.

Every major progression tier should introduce new interactions between systems.

Automation should reduce repetitive work without removing the complexity of the progression.

The player should progress by building increasingly advanced infrastructure rather than simply crafting increasingly expensive items.
